  "name": "US Broker Tax Statement (Consolidated 1099)",
  "emoji": "🧾",
  "description": "Year-end tax statement from a US broker (Form 1099 Composite / Consolidated 1099 from Schwab, Fidelity, Vanguard, E*TRADE, Merrill, Robinhood, IBKR and similar): 1099-DIV, 1099-INT, 1099-B, 1099-MISC and 1099-OID pages. Removes only what identifies the recipient: the account holder and joint holder names (in the address block or after a Recipient label), the street address and the city, state and ZIP line, the recipient's TIN or SSN (full or masked), account numbers in labeled, dashed, broker-specific and masked forms, client phone numbers and e-mails. Keeps everything you need for taxes or for an AI: box numbers and labels, all amounts, security names, CUSIPs, quantities, dates acquired and sold, proceeds, cost basis, gains and losses, wash sales, the payer's name and TIN and the broker's toll-free numbers. The broker's own street address is covered too (remove it with the X). Signatures and QR codes need a manual box.",
